To Enable Hyper-V on VM if it does not work (This is done in the host PC not in VM.). 

  

Turn on the Hyper-V features by going into “Turn Windows features on or off”. 

Also check if “Virtual Machine Platform” is checked on. 

You will need to restart to continue. 

Go into CMD as admin, type in Systeminfo.exe and go all down for information. Also go into “task manager” and click on CPU and check if “Virtualization is enabled”. 

Right click on the VM image and click on “Open VM Directory” 

Right click on the file that are marked and open with notepad ++ or a normal textpad. 

Scroll down in the text file and find vhv.enable = “TRUE” and make sure its “TRUE”. 

Go to “Core Isolation” and turn it off” and restart the computer. 

Try to turn on the VM Image with the “Virualize Intel VT-x/EPT or AMD-V/RVI” enabled. If it fails, go to CMD as admin and check Systeminfo.exe 

All down if it stands “A Hypervisor has been detected. Features required for Hyper-V will not be displayed.” We will continue… 

Type in the command: bcdedit /set hypervisorlaunchtype off 

If that worked, great!  

If this did not work, go into PowerShell as administrator. And write this command: Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName Microsoft-Hyper-V-Hypervisor 

Restart/reboot the computer and turn on the VM image and the Hyper-V installation should now work on the Windows Server 2022. 
